ence/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the expression $f(x,y) = -3xy^2.$ What are the missing entries in the following sign table of $f(x,y)?$\n\n| $y > 0$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y <                0$ |  |  |\n|  | $x<         0$ | $x> 0$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/example-9419.json" "file_sha256" "4fdc4a164e3f8e3f3670a19d46ffceeca271a16375e1219343999dde5cd1d7cd" "basis" 1104 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/c35c98904d2a0d0d6d49c582cd9f9dba9d96e91ae0da5deb2d329f38f77532e3.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/9340582eaad37c4ce1e0c8cbcdce48faec1e36c3c05adbedd61aa2de7168fd2f.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-3x$ | $y^2$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{blue}+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{blue}+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n\n \n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/743df5f5c9232346866a01aed9afa3d41fff0f61bf7812b7ae5db9a43efe59f4.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y > 0$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y <                0$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n|  | $x<         0$ | $x> 0$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/example-9419.json" "file_sha256" "4fdc4a164e3f8e3f3670a19d46ffceeca271a16375e1219343999dde5cd1d7cd" "basis" 1104 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x,y) = -6x^2y.$ Determine the region that gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y) \\geq 0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/example-9423.json" "file_sha256" "fdb93ac43769ffc58dbfbbaa3a1fa97bfbd9daacd96f411c4607f405219440ad" "basis" 1104 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/c35c98904d2a0d0d6d49c582cd9f9dba9d96e91ae0da5deb2d329f38f77532e3.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/9340582eaad37c4ce1e0c8cbcdce48faec1e36c3c05adbedd61aa2de7168fd2f.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-6x^2$ | $y$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ | $\\color{red}-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{red}-$ | $\\color{blue}+$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y) \\geq 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/assets/17dd9e10234b6a69123241a882e267d95d505d1944d7c31ef563f9ac06b990af.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/example-9423.json" "file_sha256" "fdb93ac43769ffc58dbfbbaa3a1fa97bfbd9daacd96f411c4607f405219440ad" "basis" 1104 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004890/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x,y)=-3xy.$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)\\ge 0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9b842f3a21c9451ed7f49ad5f2387423069616f45ea67dcbe5be72c834f9e7c" "basis" 1297 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/c35c98904d2a0d0d6d49c582cd9f9dba9d96e91ae0da5deb2d329f38f77532e3.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/9340582eaad37c4ce1e0c8cbcdce48faec1e36c3c05adbedd61aa2de7168fd2f.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-3x$ | $y$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/3cfdf7d548c430f225a78fa6c4d915d69207f0a1c090d13cdd530c90865731ef.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/state.json" "file_sha256" "f9b842f3a21c9451ed7f49ad5f2387423069616f45ea67dcbe5be72c834f9e7c" "basis" 1297 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3164315862af2309076c3a4ae2bfe33535f58892d2cc5690b2d16bb48f54b74a" "basis" 1297 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/r