sha256" "11c20e04272d38bd0eb1cd76248df0fd9c405b636ce7a019288b0fb863e695ff"} {"question" "q-317158" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "+"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040514/state.json" "file_sha256" "11c20e04272d38bd0eb1cd76248df0fd9c405b636ce7a019288b0fb863e695ff"} {"question" "q-121260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x,y)=-7xy.$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)\\le 0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040514/state.json" "file_sha256" "11c20e04272d38bd0eb1cd76248df0fd9c405b636ce7a019288b0fb863e695ff"} {"question" "q-121260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040514/assets/c44c38febc908fe5e941978bf44bab2e2cb4bd250765950d84f9294c9c4c9c4b.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040514/assets/209576cd78e9beb1c0f7a9bce8267163df1668a830ffc5c06918f8a726600fbe.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-7x$ | $y$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-left | $(-1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)\\le 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040514/assets/cf7fdbafdf968d3e6adfe9544a3b9e5e1736ce22fc808567f1d66fc80916534e.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040514/state.json" "file_sha256" "11c20e04272d38bd0eb1cd76248df0fd9c405b636ce7a019288b0fb863e695ff"} {"question" "q-121260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040514/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f4fa930471ee54c8dd9e34586d75f79ef528cb248505303066e48b38328455fa"} {"question" "q-121260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040514/state.json" "file_sha256" "11c20e04272d38bd0eb1cd76248df0fd9c405b636ce7a019288b0fb863e695ff"} {"question" "q-121260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040514/assets/03b7fe2ba61cbe2608c37a78c82001f6a1fdebdb59f0be0785d55ee119ba8ff4.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040514/assets/37000a15f2b6164932675c0f0e6dd78fa0ef3015dcc25b27d7dce139e8a1ce4b.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040514/assets/596e25c1d1f8a0e738d8853c17c77c2f6174a2c314a94ce1674f37b3a4c5c72b.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040514/assets/6cd862eaf47308e